Reason:
The function `retain_and_null_ptr(lh)` sets the pointer `lh` to NULL after transferring its ownership. The subsequent `dev_dbg()` call then dereferences `lh->num_descs`, which results in a NULL pointer dereference and kernel crash.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
retain_and_null_ptr(lh);
dev_dbg(&gdev->dev, "registered chardev handle for %d lines\n", handlereq.lines);
Reason:
Instead of using the now‑NULL pointer `lh`, the debug print uses `handlereq.lines`, which holds the same value as `lh->num_descs` was set to earlier. This avoids any dereference of `lh` after it has been nullified.

